+<section class="block on-white policy-page" id="top">
+  <div class="container">
+    <span class="kicker">Policies</span>
+    <h1>Website Policies</h1>
+    <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: October 13, 2026</p>
+    <p>Bayit Miklot Inc. (&ldquo;Bayit Miklot,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us&rdquo;) is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization in Dallas, Texas. This website accepts charitable donations only. This page contains all of our website policies.</p>
+    <nav class="policy-toc" aria-label="Policies on this page">
+      <ol>
+      <li><a href="#privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a></li>
+      <li><a href="#terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a></li>
+      <li><a href="#refund-policy">Refund Policy</a></li>
+      <li><a href="#cancellation-policy">Cancellation Policy</a></li>
+      <li><a href="#shipping-policy">Shipping Policy</a></li>
+      </ol>
+    </nav>
+    <section id="privacy-policy" class="policy-section">
+      <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
+<p>Bayit Miklot Inc. (&ldquo;Bayit Miklot,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us&rdquo;) respects your privacy. This policy explains what information we collect through bayitmiklot.com (the &ldquo;Site&rdquo;), how we use it, and the choices you have.</p>
+<h3>Information we collect</h3>
+<ul class="lead-line">
+  <li><strong>Information you send us.</strong> When you email or call us, we receive your name, contact details and anything you choose to share.</li>
+  <li><strong>Donation information.</strong> Card donations are processed by Stripe, Inc. Stripe collects your payment details and shares with us your name, email, billing details, donation amount and date. We never see or store your full card number. Gifts through The Donors&rsquo; Fund or other donor-advised funds are handled by those organizations, which may share your name and gift details with us.</li>
+  <li><strong>Automatic information.</strong> The Site uses the Google tag (Google Ads) to measure visits and the effectiveness of our outreach. Google may set cookies and collect information such as your IP address, browser type, pages visited and referring site.</li>
+</ul>
+<h3>Health information</h3>
+<p>Please do not send detailed medical or mental health information by email or through the Site. Email is not a secure channel. If you are seeking help, share only your contact information, and we will arrange a confidential conversation.</p>
+<h3>How we use information</h3>
+<ul class="lead-line">
+  <li>to process donations and send receipts,</li>
+  <li>to respond to inquiries and requests for help,</li>
+  <li>to thank donors and share news about our work (you may opt out at any time),</li>
+  <li>to understand and improve the Site and our outreach, and</li>
+  <li>to meet legal, accounting and tax obligations.</li>
+</ul>
+<h3>How we share information</h3>
+<p><strong>We do not sell, rent or trade your personal information.</strong> We share it only:</p>
+<ul class="lead-line">
+  <li>with service providers that help us operate (for example Stripe for payments, Google for analytics and advertising, and GitHub for website hosting),</li>
+  <li>when required by law or to protect the safety of any person, or</li>
+  <li>with your consent.</li>
+</ul>
+<h3>Cookies and your choices</h3>
+<p>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. You can limit personalized advertising at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a> and learn how Google uses data at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">policies.google.com</a>.</p>
+<p>To unsubscribe from our emails, or to ask us to access, correct or delete your information, contact us using the details below. We will respond within 30 days.</p>
+<h3>Data security and retention</h3>
+<p>We use reasonable safeguards to protect personal information. Payment data is handled by PCI-compliant processors. We keep donation records as long as required for tax and accounting purposes, and other information only as long as needed.</p>
+<h3>Children</h3>
+<p>The Site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal information.</p>
+<h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
+<p>We may update this policy from time to time. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date above shows when it last changed.</p>
+      <p class="policy-top"><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
+    </section>
+    <section id="terms-of-service" class="policy-section">
+      <h2>Terms of Service</h2>
+<p>These Terms of Service (&ldquo;Terms&rdquo;) apply to your use of bayitmiklot.com (the &ldquo;Site&rdquo;), operated by Bayit Miklot Inc. (&ldquo;Bayit Miklot,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us&rdquo;), a 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization based in Dallas, Texas. By using the Site, you agree to these Terms.</p>
+<h3>Not medical advice. In an emergency, get help now</h3>
+<p>The Site provides general information about our programs. It is not medical, psychological or clinical advice, and it does not create a provider&ndash;patient relationship. If you or someone you know is in crisis, call or text <strong>988</strong> (Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline) or call <strong>911</strong>.</p>
+<h3>Donations</h3>
+<ul class="lead-line">
+  <li>Donations are voluntary charitable gifts to Bayit Miklot Inc. and are used at our discretion to further our mission.</li>
+  <li>Card donations are processed by Stripe, Inc. Gifts through The Donors&rsquo; Fund or other donor-advised funds are processed by those organizations. Their terms also apply to those transactions.</li>
+  <li>Bayit Miklot is a 501(c)(3) organization, so donations are tax-deductible to the extent allowed by law. Please consult your tax advisor.</li>
+  <li>Refunds and cancellations are covered by our <a href="#refund-policy">Refund Policy</a> and <a href="#cancellation-policy">Cancellation Policy</a>.</li>
+  <li>You agree to use only payment methods you are authorized to use.</li>
+</ul>
+<h3>Acceptable use</h3>
+<p>You agree not to misuse the Site. For example, you may not attempt to disrupt it, gain unauthorized access to it, or use it for any unlawful purpose.</p>
+<h3>Content and trademarks</h3>
+<p>The text, photographs, logos and other content on the Site belong to Bayit Miklot or its licensors. The names &ldquo;Bayit Miklot,&rdquo; &ldquo;Home of Refuge&rdquo; and &ldquo;Community for Life&rdquo; are our marks. You may share links to the Site, but you may not copy or reuse its content for commercial purposes without our written permission.</p>
+<h3>Links to other websites</h3>
+<p>The Site links to services we do not control, such as payment processors and donor-advised fund sponsors. We are not responsible for their content or practices.</p>
+<h3>Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h3>
+<p>The Site is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; without warranties of any kind. To the fullest extent permitted by law, Bayit Miklot is not liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential damages arising from your use of the Site.</p>
+<h3>Governing law</h3>
+<p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas. Any dispute will be handled in the state or federal courts located in Dallas County, Texas.</p>
+<h3>Changes to these Terms</h3>
+<p>We may update these Terms from time to time. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date above shows when they last changed. Continued use of the Site means you accept the updated Terms.</p>
+      <p class="policy-top"><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
+    </section>
+    <section id="refund-policy" class="policy-section">
+      <h2>Refund Policy</h2>
+<p>We are grateful for every gift, and we want giving to be simple and trustworthy.</p>
+<h3>Donations are generally final</h3>
+<p>Donations are charitable gifts, and they are generally non-refundable once processed. Donations are put to work quickly to support our programs, and your receipt may be used for tax purposes.</p>
+<h3>When we will refund a donation</h3>
+<p>We will refund a donation made in error. Examples include:</p>
+<ul class="lead-line">
+  <li>a duplicate donation,</li>
+  <li>an incorrect amount (for example, an extra zero), or</li>
+  <li>a charge you did not authorize.</li>
+</ul>
+<h3>How to request a refund</h3>
+<p>Email <a href="mailto:avi@bayitmiklot.com">avi@bayitmiklot.com</a> within 30 days of the donation. Include your name, the date and amount of the donation, the last four digits of the card used, and the reason for the request.</p>
+<p>We will reply within five (5) business days. Approved refunds are issued to the original payment method. Your bank may take five to ten (5&ndash;10) business days to show the credit. When a donation is refunded, its tax receipt is no longer valid.</p>
+<p>Requests made more than 30 days after a donation are reviewed case by case.</p>
+<h3>Gifts through The Donors&rsquo; Fund or donor-advised funds</h3>
+<p>Grants from a donor-advised fund, including The Donors&rsquo; Fund, cannot be refunded to an individual donor. Please contact your fund sponsor about any error. We will work with the sponsor to correct it.</p>
+<h3>Disputed charges</h3>
+<p>If you do not recognize a charge from Bayit Miklot, please contact us before disputing it with your bank. We can usually resolve the issue faster.</p>
+      <p class="policy-top"><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
+    </section>
+    <section id="cancellation-policy" class="policy-section">
+      <h2>Cancellation Policy</h2>
+<p>This policy explains how to cancel donations made to Bayit Miklot Inc. (&ldquo;Bayit Miklot&rdquo;) through this website.</p>
+<h3>One-time donations</h3>
+<p>A one-time donation is processed immediately, so it cannot be cancelled once it is complete. If you made a mistake, please see our <a href="#refund-policy">Refund Policy</a>.</p>
+<h3>Recurring donations</h3>
+<p>If you set up a recurring (for example, monthly) donation, you may cancel it at any time. To cancel:</p>
+<ul class="lead-line">
+  <li>use the link to manage your donation in your email receipt, if one is provided, or</li>
+  <li>email <a href="mailto:avi@bayitmiklot.com">avi@bayitmiklot.com</a> or call 917-676-2014 with your name, the email used for the donation, and the amount.</li>
+</ul>
+<p>Please contact us at least three (3) business days before your next scheduled payment. We will confirm the cancellation by email. A cancellation stops future payments. It does not refund payments already made.</p>
+<h3>Gifts through The Donors&rsquo; Fund or donor-advised funds</h3>
+<p>Grants and recurring grants made through The Donors&rsquo; Fund or another donor-advised fund are controlled by that sponsoring organization. Please contact your fund sponsor to cancel or change them.</p>
+      <p class="policy-top"><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
+    </section>
+    <section id="shipping-policy" class="policy-section">
+      <h2>Shipping Policy</h2>
+<h3>No physical goods</h3>
+<p>We do not sell products, and we do not ship physical goods. No shipping charges apply to any transaction on this website.</p>
+<h3>Donation receipts</h3>
+<p>When you donate by card, a receipt is sent to the email address you provide at checkout, usually within minutes. Receipts for gifts made through The Donors&rsquo; Fund or a donor-advised fund are issued by that sponsoring organization.</p>
+<p>If you did not receive your receipt, please check your spam folder, then contact us and we will resend it.</p>
+      <p class="policy-top"><a href="#top">Back to top</a></p>
+    </section>
+    <section id="contact" class="policy-section">
+      <h2>Contact us</h2>
+      <p>Questions about any of these policies, or requests about your donation or personal information, can be sent to:</p>
+      <p><strong>Bayit Miklot Inc.</strong><br>Dallas, Texas<br>Email: <a href="mailto:avi@bayitmiklot.com">avi@bayitmiklot.com</a><br>Phone: <a href="tel:917-676-2014">917-676-2014</a></p>
+    </section>
+  </div>
+</section>
